Do not build AppStream's man pages.

AppStream 1.0.6 includes docs/ unconditionally, and docs/meson.build runs
`xsltproc --nonet` against the Docbook man page stylesheet and calls error() if
that fails. The pages document appstreamcli, which the runtime does not ship;
libadwaita links libappstream for metadata parsing only. Satisfying the check
would put a documentation toolchain into the build image for output that is
pruned from the shipped tree.

Dropping the subdir leaves data/, which still uses itstool, and every library
target untouched. Nothing to send upstream: it is a local choice not to build a
documentation target. Drop it when AppStream gains an option for the man pages.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -226,7 +226,6 @@
 subdir('po/')
 subdir('data/')
 subdir('contrib/')
-subdir('docs/')
 subdir('tests/')
 if get_option('qt')
     subdir('qt/')
